<article class="env-definition" id="002I">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/002I">Definition <span data-tag="002I">4.14.6</span>.</a> Suppose that $I$ is a set, and suppose given for every $i \in I$ an object $M_ i$ of the category $\mathcal{C}$. A <em>product</em> $\prod _{i\in I} M_ i$ is by definition $\mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits _\mathcal {I} M$ (if it exists) where $\mathcal{I}$ is the category having only identities as morphisms and having the elements of $I$ as objects. </p>
</article>